uch as sunflower seeds, linseeds or pumpkin seeds. Most Danes eat rugbrød every day."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-rugbr-d"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rugbr%C3%B8d"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Danish cuisine","cuisine/danish-cuisine",[["Smørrebrød","dish/sm-rrebr-d"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Cold cut","ingredient/cold-cut"],["Garnish (cooking)","ingredient/garnish-cooking"],["Lunch meat","ingredient/lunch-meat"],["Spread","ingredient/spread"]]}]},"dish/spundekas":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/spundekas","n":"Spundekäs","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Spundekäs [ˈʃpʊndəˌkɛːs] is a spiced cream cheese spread originating from the German region of Northern Rhenish Hesse. Often served as an appetizer (especially at Straußenwirtschaften) or at gatherings, usually along with lye rolls or soft pretzels as well as regional wine, it remains a symbol of regional cultural expression."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-spundekas"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spundek%C3%A4s"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"],["Thuringian cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine-thuringia"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Fresh cheese","ingredient/fresh-cheese"],["Quark","ingredient/quark"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Quick German Recipes","ref":"site/quick-german-recipes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"quick-german-recipes.com","note":"Long-running site by German-born cook Gerhild Fulson (Oma) with traditional German home recipes.","url":"https://www.quick-german-recipes.com/about-me.html","suggested":true},{"name":"Dirndl Kitchen","ref":"site/dirndlkitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dirndlkitchen.com","note":"Blog o